cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MarkerFlow, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "MarkerFlow: a generalised, marker-agnostic metabarcoding pipeline"
abstract: >-
  MarkerFlow is a reproducible Illumina paired-end amplicon metabarcoding
  pipeline (merge, quality check, primer trimming, DADA2 ASV inference, and
  taxonomy assignment) that is configurable for any marker, with ready-to-use
  configurations for 18S (protists), ITS (fungi), and 16S (bacteria/archaea).
  It also includes a downstream statistics stage (filtering, rarefaction, and
  dataset-quality diagnostics).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singer
    given-names: David
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # <- add your ORCID
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-18"
license: MIT
